          "distinct": false,
          "id": "0e147d43041e8782a4b88cedd6f92d98414082ed",
          "message": "perf(sparq-geo): id-level indexed-universe fast path for the spatial FILTER pushdown (sq-7jt80) (#1847)\n\n* perf(geo): id-level indexed-universe fast path for the spatial FILTER pushdown (sq-7jt80) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe `geof:sfWithin`/`sfIntersects`/`distance` FILTER pushdown's answer-safety\nguard (`apply_spatial_pushdown`) resolved EVERY non-candidate row's binding to a\n`Term` and hashed it into an `FxHashSet<Term>` (via `is_indexed`) — ~one WKT\n`String` allocation + Term hash per non-candidate row, which dominated the query\non a large corpus. Make that keep decision ID-LEVEL: the same verdict as a pure\n`FxHashSet<Id>` lookup on the scanned column, ZERO per-row Term materialisation.\n\n- sparq-geo `GeoIndex`: capture the source `Graph::dict` address at `build` as an\n  opaque freshness token (`dict_ptr`), thread each entry's `geo:asWKT` OBJECT id\n  into a new `pub Entry::literal_id`, and maintain the live literal-id set\n  (`literal_ids`, refcounted by owning-feature so a shared geometry id leaves only\n  on its last entry) in lockstep with `slots`/`free` across `insert_entry` and the\n  `apply_delta` drop loop. New `pub fn indexed_ids_for(dict_ptr) -> Option<&FxHashSet<Id>>`\n  returns the set ONLY on a dict-address match (else `None`); `apply_delta`\n  invalidates freshness if the graph's dict address moved.\n- sparq-engine `SpatialProvider`: new `indexed_ids(dict_ptr) -> Option<Arc<FxHashSet<Id>>>`\n  with a DEFAULT `None` (existing providers unaffected); documents the freshness\n  contract and that `set.contains(&i)` MUST equal `is_indexed(&dict.term(i))`.\n- sparq-geo `GeoIndexProvider`: implements it, delegating freshness to the index\n  and handing out a cached `Arc` (no per-call realloc).\n- engine `apply_spatial_pushdown`: FAST path (pure integer lookups) when\n  `indexed_ids(dict_ptr)` is `Some`; the EXISTING per-row `term_of_id`/`is_indexed`\n  fallback UNCHANGED when `None`. Both branches share one keep predicate:\n  `cand_ids.contains(&id) || !indexed.contains(&id)`.\n\nAnswer-safety invariant HELD: result is byte-identical to the per-row path and the\nno-index post-hoc path — a binding the index has no opinion on (non-`geo:asWKT`\npredicate, non-geographic CRS, different graph, stale dict) is NEVER dropped.\nsparq-core UNTOUCHED; no new cargo feature (rides the default-on pushdown seam).\n\nTests (all non-vacuous — mutation-verified): 3 direct unit tests for\n`indexed_ids_for` (fresh-dict content == `id_of` of the reported literal terms;\ndict-mismatch declines; shared-geometry-id refcount survives one owner's delete);\ntests/index.rs delta consistency assertion (maintained id-set == fresh build);\ntests/pushdown.rs `compare3` differential — no-index vs the id-level FAST path vs a\n`NoIdLevelProvider` forcing the per-row SLOW fallback — over a pure geo:asWKT\ncolumn, mixed indexed/unindexed bindings, a non-geographic asWKT literal (CRS\nsafety, kept then declined by the exact FILTER), a non-indexed single-column\nmatching binding (discriminates the fast path — catches the dropped-non-candidate\nmutant), and post-`apply_delta`.\n\nGates (both feature states GREEN): clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings;\ncargo test -p sparq-geo (default AND geosparql_rewrite,reproject) incl.\nogc_compliance_ratchet; cargo test -p sparq-engine (286 lib + all integration, 0\nfailed); RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --all-features\nclean; bench/geo/run.sh count gate — all 6 workloads == expected.tsv (geof_within\n1526, geo_compliance_pass 25, unchanged); readme-template 0 deviations.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci(geo): declare intentional feature-OFF wasm-bundle delta for the spatial-pushdown id-level fast path (sq-7jt80) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe id-level answer-safety fast path in PR #1847 is an always-compiled\nsparq-engine change (SpatialProvider::indexed_ids default method + the\napply_spatial_pushdown integer-lookup retain branch), so the byte-for-byte\nfeature-OFF wasm-bundle equality gate (vectorized-feature-off leg 2) correctly\nobserves a +~1217-byte (+~0.077%) delta. Declare the intent per mechanism V2\n(bench/feature-off-declarations/README.md): result is byte-identical to the\nper-row path, delta is within the 2% bench.yml band so no\nmetrics.wasm_bundle_bytes floor raise is needed. 🤖 SPARQ agent\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <jw896977@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
